				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Extract Cocoon namespace maps, Mountain dispatchers\n\nAdvance three Element submodules with structural extractions, runtime fixes, and formatting alignment.\n\n**Cocoon** lifts the inline RegisterCustomEditor function and six shared registry maps (CustomEditorProviders, CustomEditorProvidersByViewType, TreeDataProviders, TreeDataProvidersByViewId, WebviewViewProviders, WebviewViewBuilders, WebviewPanels) from Namespace.ts into dedicated RegisterCustomEditor.ts and Registry.ts modules. Namespace.ts shrinks by ~170 lines and re-exports the relocated maps through the existing path, preserving all provider registration and lifecycle behaviour unchanged.\n\n**Mountain** extracts the 1400-line `process_mountain_request` and 600-line `send_mountain_notification` match blocks from CocoonService/mod.rs into GenericRequest::Dispatcher and GenericNotification::Dispatcher modules, reducing mod.rs by ~1900 lines and clarifying the gRPC service boundary. Three fixes accompany the refactor: (1) scope the MutexGuard on WorkspaceFolders to a block so it is dropped before any await point, restoring Send-ness for tauri::async_runtime::spawn; (2) replace the OnceLock that caches a permanent None (routing all dev logs to /tmp after the first failed resolution) with a two-phase RESOLVED/RETRY system that retries after Tauri creates the app-data directory; (3) replace a bare `return Ok(...)` inside a WindServiceHandlers match arm (which exited the enclosing async block and broke Scheduler::Submit's `Output = ()` bound) with an if/else expression. A clippy-nit removing redundant `.as_str()` in AliasPath.rs is included. Two follow-up style commits normalize dispatcher indentation and update Cargo.toml/tauri.conf.json build identifiers for the dev profile.\n\n**Worker** normalises indentation across all three ESBuild configuration files to hard tabs via two style-only commits (spaces → tabs, then tabs → fully aligned tabs). Zero functional changes — build output is identical.\n\nAll Target/ compiled artifacts and RouteManifest files are regenerated for Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "a74c89e53e1c6310ff031e05dafc682fd0b0c121"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:38:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Extract Cocoon extension host, wire hierarchy RPC, fix IPC\n\nAdvance Cocoon, Mountain, and Sky submodules in a coordinated round-trip that decomposes the extension host monolith, adds missing IPC endpoints for call/type hierarchy, and fixes data accuracy across the whole pipeline.\n\n**Cocoon** splits the ~1500-line inline extension host handler into three focused modules — VscodeModuleHooks.ts, EnsureVscodeAPI.ts, ActivateExtension.ts — reducing Handler.ts to a thin dispatch layer. Five real-world extension compatibility issues are fixed alongside the refactor: Copilot dist-preflight so missing build artifacts don't crash activation; `context.extension.packageJSON` populated from the real manifest on disk (`@vscode/extension-telemetry` reads `aiKey`); workspace config cache seeded from `contributes.configuration.properties` before `activate()` runs (prevents GitLens TypeError on nested config access); `activate()` return value backfilled into the registry so `vscode.extensions.getExtension(id).exports` resolves; POJO-tolerant `RelativePattern` wrapper added (fixes Shopify.ruby-lsp activation). Six missing VS Code API enums (`LogLevel`, `OverviewRulerLane`, `UIKind`, `TextEditorCursorStyle`, `DebugConfigurationProviderTriggerKind`, `IndentAction`) are now defined — extensions referencing them at module-load time crashed with undefined. `willSaveTextDocument` now batches `waitUntil` thenables into a single `window.applyTextEdits` call matching VS Code's `acceptWillSaveDocument` ordering. Configuration cache supports a `\"*\"` sentinel for full model rebuild on bulk settings writes.\n\n**Mountain** adds language-scoped configuration overrides — `UpdateValue` writes into `\"[<langId>]\"` scoped keys matching the VS Code convention used by prettier-vscode, vscode-eslint, and other per-language formatters. A `OnceLock`-backed static session ID replaces per-call `Uuid::new_v4()`, so extensions comparing `telemetryInfo.sessionId` across initialization calls see a consistent process-lifetime value. `CocoonService` dispatches `$provideCallHierarchyItems`/`prepareCallHierarchy` and `$provideTypeHierarchyItems`/`prepareTypeHierarchy` to the respective providers, unblocking F12 / Go to References / Call Hierarchy in the editor. Three `mountain_*` IPC stubs return real data: `mountain_get_configuration` yields the live merged config, `mountain_get_services_status` reports actual Cocoon connection state, `mountain_get_state` surfaces real workspace folder count and active document URI. SOCKS proxy env-var parsing emits the correct PAC keyword (`SOCKS` for socks URIs, `PROXY` for http/https). Dev-log dedup switches from `lock()` to `try_lock()` so a contended mutex never parks a Tokio worker. Always-on-top toggle moves from a heuristic title-prefix proxy to a `static AtomicBool`, correctly flipping state on each invocation. The `window.didChangeTextEditorSelection` Vine notification now includes `viewColumn` from incoming arguments, so extensions calling `activeTextEditor.viewColumn` see the correct pane number in split-editor layouts. A follow-up formatting commit normalizes brace placement and comment reflow across four files.\n\n**Sky** replaces the hardcoded `viewColumn: 1` in `sky:editor:activeChanged` and `sky:editor:selectionChanged` IPC payloads with a `GetViewColumn()` helper that reads `EditorGroups.activeGroup.index` (0-based) and converts to the 1-based view column the VS Code API expects, safely falling back to 1 when the EditorGroups service isn't yet available.\n\nExtension host reliability and IPC data accuracy are materially improved across all three layers of the round-trip.",
			"SHA": "3e397f73d617f23b3da7e170f7405fd4af1b8176"
		},
